# Replaced wholesale by the slax-kitchen `enable-ssh` recipe.
#
# Slackware has no /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/ and the stock sshd_config carries no
# Include directive, so a drop-in fragment is not possible -- unlike Debian, which
# ships sshd_config.d/root_login_enable.conf and needs no change here.
#
# The three non-comment lines below are upstream Slax's, unchanged. The fourth is the
# point of the file: without an explicit PermitRootLogin, OpenSSH 9.5 defaults to
# prohibit-password, so enabling sshd on stock Slax gives you a daemon that root -- the
# only account with a password -- cannot log into.
AuthorizedKeysFile	.ssh/authorized_keys
UsePAM yes
Subsystem	sftp	/usr/libexec/sftp-server

PermitRootLogin yes
